  "notes": "West leads the ♣K against 4♠. The defense gets off to a good start, cashing 2 rounds of clubs and taking a club ruff. East switches to diamonds. South must win the ♦A.\n\nSouth must hope that North's fourth heart can provide a discard for South's diamond loser. South should begin by drawing trump. When East follows twice, the count on the hand is known. East started with 3 spades, 7 diamonds (for his preempt), and 2 clubs. He must have exactly 1 heart.\n\nGiven that hearts are 5-1, the only hope is that East's heart is the ♥K. South should play a heart to the ♥A. When East co-operates by dropping the ♥K, South can take 4 heart tricks by finessing against West's ♥10.",
